option: buildable-host no
---

# platform.pizero.sdcard

The RP2350-PiZero's TF socket, wired for four-bit SDIO and used here in SPI mode through
mm.sdcard: SPI1: clock GP30, MOSI GP31 (CMD), MISO GP40 (DAT0), chip select GP43 (DAT3), from
Waveshare's RP2350-PiZero schematic -- pins only the RP2350B has, which is why
the board builds against the SDK's own PiZero header. rp2350_pizero binds it
and rp2350_pizero_usb_host inherits it. The card runs at 25 MHz once identified, which the Pico's
SPI divider rounds down to what it holds.
